{"record_id": "23430906", "status": "PASS", "disposition_by": "root", "created_utc": "2026-10-25T05:28:51.440044+00:00", "approved_scope": "Full literal Theorem1: fixed H in(1/4,1), independent standard equal-H fBm, both complete deterministic uniform grids including terminalT, everyT>0, integern>=1 and everyL2 estimator including nonlinear, RMS(canonical iterated area minus estimator)>= exact published positive c_H*T^(2H)*n^(1/2-2H).", "root_clearance": "Later root scientific disposition only. Exact original reviewer objects and the original scope pending fields remain preserved. Website rendering, live, browser and native tracker gates are not passed by this config.", "root_clearance_file": "verification/root-clearance-23430906-20261025.json", "root_clearance_sha256": "86a8ceed51423cf9c79c71b41389c644361d9b75b54b6bce9093ff9fa0307e8d", "root_clearance_record": {"utc": "2026-10-25T05:24:56.257770+00:00", "record_id": "23430906", "sheet_row": 82, "status": "PASS_REWRITTEN", "disposition_by": "root", "approved_scope": "Full literal Theorem1: fixed H in(1/4,1), independent standard equal-H fBm, both complete deterministic uniform grids including terminalT, everyT>0, integern>=1 and everyL2 estimator including nonlinear, RMS(canonical iterated area minus estimator)>= exact published positive c_H*T^(2H)*n^(1/2-2H).", "root_reading": "# Root assessment of the actual seven-page Gaussian-witness manuscript\n\nRoot read the full actual deposited PDF (all seven pages, not merely inventory text) and proof-bearing manuscript TeX before reading the three complete final reports. Then read scope REVIEW and claim-boundary map; analytic REVIEW, independent derivation, explicit correction addendum and exact verdict; adversarial REVIEW and exact verdict. Reader page4 was visually inspected to resolve the Fourier conjugation and complete Gram formula. Actual NTU institutional journal-formatted pages223,226,229-230,237-240 were read, including entire relevant Theorem2 proof; Proposition6 page229 visually inspected. Established canonical existence is a checked imported theorem interface, not a reconstruction of all historical background theory.\n\nThe exact claim is for fixed H in (1/4,1), independent centered standard equal-H fBm, both complete uniform grids of n scalar observations EACH including T, every T>0, integer n>=1, and every L2 grid estimator. The canonical iterated integral has RMS error >= 2*pi*a/[D_H sqrt(Pbar_f Pbar_g)] T^(2H)n^(1/2-2H). It includes nonlinear estimators without assuming their polynomial form.\n\nIndependent root reasoning: standard Gaussian realization gives exact covariance from normalized K_t; conjugating hat h in u_h restores h(t)-h(0), not a reflected bump. f=phi' and g=phi zero extensions have traces zero through order2, hence the third weak derivatives have no boundary atoms; integration by parts yields Fourier decay min(L,N|xi|^-3). With alpha=2H+1, scaled bump norms cancel cell size. Periodization has bounded central term pi^alpha L^2 and two tails controlled by the decreasing odd series <=1+1/[2(5-alpha)], then finite trigonometric Parseval gives M=D_H Pbar/(2pi). This is an upper Gram bound, not the invalid rough-increment lower coercivity. Orthogonality of ALL witness coordinates to ALL observed coordinates gives joint Gaussian independence of the whole vector. Coordinate independence gives EY^2=tr(AC), and PSD ordering gives <=n M_f M_g without entrywise positivity or commutation. Fixed n,T,j left-sum refinement gives deterministic pairing integral f_j g_j'=a Delta^(2H); a=4/45045>0. The positive sum n*a*Delta^(2H) then proves the exact constant by Cauchy-Schwarz. All-L2 F follows from grid independence; equality in joint law with the finite observation vector transfers to an arbitrary original model. Auxiliary noises need not be original-path measurable.\n\nCanonical bridge: finite polygonal identity P_m=L_m+Q_m and independent coordinate increment covariance give EQ_m^2=T^(4H)m^-4H[m+2sum(m-r)rho(r)^2]/4. The second-difference bound for r>=2 gives the three summation regimes: m^(1-4H),m^-2 logm,m^-2, all vanish on H>1/4. Thus canonical polygonal existence suffices independently of any exact Euler coefficient. The manuscript's separated-cell covariance bound also follows because derivative covariances have fixed sign away from diagonal, their product is nonnegative, distance >=r-1 and triangle product volume1/4. Same/adjacent cells use finite c0 and Cauchy-Schwarz only.\n\nRoot does not adopt the first analytic review's excluded-H=1 mistake: actual Q_m=T^2 Z1Z2/(2m), EQ_m^2=T^4/(4m^2), as the preserved correction explicitly derives. Endpoint failure of the positive lower bound is instead due to recoverability and divergent D_H. This was a review-control error; source paper is unchanged and correct. At H=1/4 nonnegative diagonalT/4 prevents this bridge. Brownian conditional optimum T/(2sqrt(n)) is prior; witness bound weaker. n=1 works directly. Halved antisymmetric area differs by observed product and retains optimal residual; unhalved difference doubles it.\n\nThe actual NTU Theorem2/Remark10 construction interfaces match standard independent coordinates and canonical polygonal iterated orientation. No formal proof of the entire32page upstream theory or every exact coefficient is claimed. No journal-byte identity or journal-error claim follows from the pinned arXiv-v1 criticism. Historical novelty/theorem-method priority/current worldwide openness and inaccessible Dickinson/Jackowski broader implications remain UNKNOWN as explicitly printed. Those literature gaps do not supply a missing logical step in this direct proof. Public wording must preserve prior Brownian/smooth rates and Fourier-projection credit, with no firstness claim. Finite controls are corroboration, not universal proof.\n\nConclusion: full literal Theorem1 passes for page preparation; no substantive central defect or gap found. No source repairs or scope reductions. Follow-up null. AI review is not human peer review or formal machine certification. Actual editorial/render/live/browser/native-URL gates still remain.\n", "source_receipt_sha256": "814617d4e7941126dd052a918a66e12e9460d58e55ba6c9edb58da82c1f22443", "root_custody_receipt": "papers/23430906/reviews/root/root-custody-recheck.json", "root_custody_receipt_sha256": "8300ef8d51515eda7767e2d6ab58ceb400a055693cf3b0b95c8cf4e5857547cf", "root_final_seal_bindings_rehashed": 560, "root_extracted_outer_members_compared": 225, "pdf_sha256": "33b90a4d846db58ea93efd453c13455fbeb3a29dcaa3e4cc49a68c0a8ebdff5b", "supplement_sha256": "4e4a1b20c2da7f5a6e686256f7f8d7bba9c8db71e21f316f99da63285f7b0191", "source_tex_sha256": "4ffbe0d65609213fd91aecf675661ff278e4e1bd5037db8836f1291f5bdc1d78", "reviews": {"scope": {"report": "papers/23430906/reviews/scope/REVIEW.md", "report_sha256": "2706772185d638c405630bd18649185bdd1fb43ae8b818d05b8d683632970c83", "verdict": "papers/23430906/reviews/scope/verdict.json", "verdict_sha256": "76860100de668ecd878d1952d800c1818ca291a55cba95053e944004532db25a"}, "analytic": {"report": "papers/23430906/reviews/analytic/REVIEW.md", "report_sha256": "564ffaea304c7897d043e12609e87a08f922330c189010bc3a1abec22155f936", "verdict": "papers/23430906/reviews/analytic/verdict.json", "verdict_sha256": "a750ed5e6e8ca6dd7a85b44dc20909ca2db34e739b31f06aa4828fee6ddd8e7e"}, "adversarial": {"report": "papers/23430906/reviews/adversarial/REVIEW.md", "report_sha256": "288b002defd605f81f27cdc14b8abda6e162518e28f2de5d1296220c0dc0b68d", "verdict": "papers/23430906/reviews/adversarial/verdict.json", "verdict_sha256": "8b1becfb2d48dd46fd77cb88a39af28dc885fdb26e3980bb1778536ca3f5847b"}}, "reviewed_zenodo_version": "1.0", "publication_date": "2026-10-14", "record_created_utc": "2026-10-17T05:14:35.437960+00:00", "review_limits": ["Imported canonical-area existence checked at actual NTU Prop6/Remark10/Theorem2 and full relevant proof; no reproof of all background stochastic theory.", "Full priority, novelty, current worldwide openness and broader inaccessible Dickinson/Jackowski implications UNKNOWN. Do not promote as first solution/new general method.", "Prior exact Brownian optimum and smooth-range asymptotic rate, Fourier localization/Gaussian projection antecedents credited.", "No sharp constant/exact limit/law/H-uniform/endpoints/nonuniform/adaptive/unequal-H/correlated extension. n counts observations per component.", "Canonical iterated versus halved/unhalved antisymmetric conventions have different factors as specified.", "The first analytic review self-correction for excludedH1 is explicit and preserved; no source-paper repair.", "Finite computations and original code diagnostic checks are not universal analytic proof/interval arithmetic/human peer review/formal certification.", "No journal-error allegation or publisher-byte identity from pinned arXivv1 source critique. Public copy can keep source-version detail brief."], "scope_gate_resolution": "Scope pending mathematical verdict preserved; complete analytic/adversarial and root actual-proof assessment resolve scientific gate without rescoping.", "source_repair": false, "human_peer_review": false, "formal_machine_verification": false, "follow_up": null, "authorization": "Prepare source-bound publication/promotion only. Preserve full original abstract/date/version/claims and attribution. Render/live/browser/native AA gates remain; AA blank untilverifiedlive."}, "pdf_sha256": "33b90a4d846db58ea93efd453c13455fbeb3a29dcaa3e4cc49a68c0a8ebdff5b", "supplement_sha256": "4e4a1b20c2da7f5a6e686256f7f8d7bba9c8db71e21f316f99da63285f7b0191", "publication_sha256": "48aa3177f3105e68f61dda74b7d4b06ed414b8ec9e86a8184bc431d4e0c888dd", "source_receipt_sha256": "814617d4e7941126dd052a918a66e12e9460d58e55ba6c9edb58da82c1f22443", "source_receipt_record": {"record_id": "23430906", "retrieved_utc": "2026-10-25T05:12:53.843647+00:00", "record_url": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23430906", "record_raw_bytes": 6040, "record_raw_sha256": "50b895ad